  <div class="bg-[#111] border border-white/5 rounded-2xl p-8 max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 mb-16">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Our Verdict</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">UpCloud is the right pick for developers who care about predictable I/O performance and want a clean API on top of their VPS. The maxIOPS guarantee is real — it's enforced at the hypervisor layer, not best-effort like most competitors. For database workloads, container hosts, and CI runners where random read/write IOPS matter, UpCloud is a tier above generic "NVMe-equipped" hosts. The trade-off is price: $5/mo for the smallest plan is twice Vultr's $2.50 and 2.5x RackNerd's $1.99. If budget is the constraint, look at RackNerd or Vultr. If predictable I/O is the constraint, UpCloud is the best in its tier.</p>
